  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25218780",
      "title": "Key Feature: File-based Routing",
      "lectureOrder": 418,
      "videoOrder": 385,
      "sourceHash": "b69f3f5fd1609ab508b44d2515a56ada9277a93c0eceaf5200a9de670ec2e0e4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.209,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "Another very nice feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 9.04,
          "en": "added by NextJS is file-based routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.04,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "Now what does this mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "In traditional React, you don't even have a router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 16.04,
          "en": "And just to be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.04,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "routing means that we give the user the illusion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.71,
          "en": "of having multiple pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.71,
          "end": 24.91,
          "en": "When we navigate around and we load different pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.91,
          "end": 27.29,
          "en": "then that's the job of a router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.29,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "Typically we use React Router for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 34.94,
          "en": "This router basically watches the URL, and when it changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.94,
          "end": 37.48,
          "en": "it basically prevents the browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.48,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "of sending a request to some backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "and instead renders different content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 44.89,
          "en": "on the page with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.89,
          "end": 47.33,
          "en": "A different component in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.33,
          "end": 48.82,
          "en": "That's what routing is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.82,
          "end": 51.02,
          "en": "We change what's visible on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.02,
          "end": 55.6,
          "en": "based on the URL without sending a extra request to a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.6,
          "end": 58.97,
          "en": "because we stay in that single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.97,
          "end": 62.03,
          "en": "which we typically build with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.03,
          "end": 65.27,
          "en": "Now that's routing, and typically with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.27,
          "end": 67.33,
          "en": "routing is set up in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.33,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "That code could look something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "depending on the version of React Router you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 76.13,
          "en": "Now this works and it's not bad, not wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.13,
          "end": 78.22,
          "en": "React Router is a great package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.22,
          "end": 81.06,
          "en": "but it is extra code which you have to write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 85.09,
          "en": "And then often you end up storing your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.09,
          "end": 89.33,
          "en": "that act as pages in a separate folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.33,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "which kind of replicates your route set up in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 97.78,
          "en": "So if you have three pages set up as pages and code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.78,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "you have three page components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "in that pages component folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "Makes sense, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 104.89,
          "en": "Now since that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.89,
          "end": 109.3,
          "en": "NextJS gets rid of that in-code route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.3,
          "end": 110.87,
          "en": "Instead, with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.87,
          "end": 115.2,
          "en": "you would define pages and routes with files and folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 119.66,
          "en": "You have a special pages folder in NextJS apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.66,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "which has to be named pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 126.08,
          "en": "and then you are structuring that folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.08,
          "end": 130.73,
          "en": "defines the routes and paths your page supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.73,
          "end": 131.563,
          "en": "And of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.563,
          "end": 135.43,
          "en": "we're also going to learn how that works in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.43,
          "end": 138.79,
          "en": "Now that simply allows us to get rid of that extra code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.79,
          "end": 140.57,
          "en": "and hence we have to write less code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.57,
          "end": 144.53,
          "en": "we have less work, and it's a highly understandable concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.53,
          "end": 145.94,
          "en": "because it's very close",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.94,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "to how we all started with web development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 152.2,
          "en": "When you're getting started with just HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.2,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "and CSS and some basic JavaScript maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 157.6,
          "en": "then you build basic websites",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.6,
          "end": 160.15,
          "en": "by adding multiple HTML files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.15,
          "end": 162.46,
          "en": "and the names of these files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.46,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "or the folders in which they sit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 167.9,
          "en": "define how you can navigate between these files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.9,
          "end": 170.21,
          "en": "How you can link these files together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.21,
          "end": 173.6,
          "en": "And NextJS basically allows us to go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.6,
          "end": 178.6,
          "en": "to this very basic, yet understandable concept of routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.7,
          "end": 182.77,
          "en": "And NextJS still supports all the features we might want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.77,
          "end": 187.06,
          "en": "like nested routes or dynamic routes with dynamic parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.06,
          "end": 188.02,
          "en": "and all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.02,
          "end": 191.203,
          "en": "And we're going to see that in this course, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
